course: dictionary
lesson: 3377
title: Exhibit: to show, or a thing on show
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Exhibit can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, to exhibit means to show things to the public, often in a museum or gallery. As a noun, an exhibit is one object on show. «In a museum you do not touch exhibits unless signs say you can, because they can be old and fragile.» Here exhibits are the objects on show, and fragile means easily broken.
explain: Use the context to choose. A museum, a gallery and a science fair are places where things are shown, so exhibit links to showing things. Try your meaning in the sentence: «do not touch the things on show unless signs say you can» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Exhibit has another meaning: to show a feeling or sign. «The dog exhibited fear.» The dog is not in a museum here. It is showing that it is scared. In science, animals exhibit behaviours, which means they show certain ways of acting.
fact: Exhibit can be a verb (to show things to others) or a noun (one object on show).
fact: «Exhibit» can also mean a whole exhibition in the USA, as in «a dinosaur exhibit».
fact: «Exhibit» can mean to show a feeling or sign, as in «the dog exhibited fear».
fact: In court, an exhibit is a piece of evidence, such as «Exhibit A».
fact: Useful phrases: on exhibit, museum exhibit, interactive exhibit, exhibit signs of.
exercise: «In a museum you do not touch exhibits unless signs say you can.» What is an exhibit in this sentence? | *An object on show | A ticket to get in | A person who guards the door | A rule about being quiet
exercise: «The dog exhibited fear.» What does exhibited mean? | *Showed | Forgot | Ran away from | Hid from
exercise: Find and copy one word that means easily broken in «In a museum you do not touch exhibits unless signs say you can, because they can be old and fragile.» | museum | exhibits | *fragile | signs
test: Ms Shah says, «We will exhibit our science projects on Friday.» What does exhibit mean here? | To hide away | To take home | *To show to others | To measure carefully
test: In court, «Exhibit A» is shown to the judge. What is an exhibit in court? | *A piece of evidence | A funny story | A type of animal | A judge's seat
exam: Which sentence uses exhibit as a verb, meaning to show? | The exhibit is near the door. | *«We will exhibit our paintings in the hall.» | The museum exhibit is closed today. | The exhibit was a dinosaur bone.
